1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,540
Welcome to David Research Monitor.

2
00:00:02,580 --> 00:00:04,780
In the next few minutes, you'll see how it turns

3
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:08,460
the topics you care about into a focused research brief.

4
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:11,180
Everything on screen is fictional sample data.

5
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:16,320
First, connect DokoBot's browser bridge and check the connection.

6
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:19,840
Research Monitor checks it before each run, so you'll know

7
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:23,680
when it's ready. If your browser requests extension access,

8
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:24,640
approve it there.

9
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:28,980
Next, choose how you want the findings analyzed.

10
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:32,740
Use LM Studio to keep analysis local, bring your own

11
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:36,340
OpenAI API key, or sign in to Codex with an

12
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:40,660
eligible ChatGPT account. Research Monitor doesn't save either

13
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:41,540
credential.

14
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:45,160
Now, add a topic you care about.

15
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:48,120
Give it a few phrases that signal a good match,

16
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:50,760
and exclude terms that create noise.

17
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:54,760
You can also fine-tune its sources, result age, and volume.

18
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:58,700
Set the days and time that work for you, then

19
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:00,460
choose the topics to monitor.

20
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:03,980
You can run the full analysis or collect links first.

21
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:06,860
When you're happy with the setup, enable the schedule.

22
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:11,000
LinkedIn's DokoBot read block starts on.

23
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:15,040
Your scheduled scans can still discover relevant public links,

24
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:18,560
while reads of LinkedIn pages through DokoBot stay blocked.

25
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:23,380
Switch the block off to allow multi-page LinkedIn reads during

26
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:27,060
scheduled scans and for URL batches you choose.

27
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:30,900
This setting controls Research Monitor's requests to DokoBot.

28
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:33,780
Check LinkedIn's rules before enabling it.

29
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:36,680
Already have a post in mind?

30
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:40,280
Open Capture, choose a topic, and add one or more

31
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:44,360
URLs. You can ask DokoBot to capture those pages, or

32
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:46,360
paste the visible text yourself.

33
00:01:47,660 --> 00:01:51,500
When you're ready, choose Run Now for discovery and AI

34
00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:55,900
analysis. Discover Links Only creates a faster report without

35
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:59,340
AI. On Home, you can follow the run and open

36
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:00,540
earlier reports.

37
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:03,920
The report starts with a quick scorecard.

38
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:08,480
Discovered counts candidate items; New Relevant shows fresh

39
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:13,920
matches. Analyzed counts items reviewed by your chosen AI provider,

40
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
and Duplicates shows repeated material removed from the results.

41
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:23,340
Each result card shows its source, topic, relevance, and a

42
00:02:23,380 --> 00:02:25,700
concise summary of why it matched.

43
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:28,180
Relevance is the fit to your topic.

44
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:31,300
Open Original takes you straight to the source.

45
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:36,600
In Reports, you can open or export the standalone HTML

46
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:40,640
report. Bookmark anything worth keeping in the table below.

47
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:44,200
Bookmarked items remain available through automatic cleanup.

48
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:48,540
For your first run, keep the topic narrow and check

49
00:02:48,580 --> 00:02:53,660
a few original links. If AI is temporarily unavailable, Research

50
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:57,820
Monitor preserves the discoveries and explains what was deferred.

51
00:02:57,900 --> 00:03:00,540
Your local HTML report is still there.
